{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/605017-what-are-you-best-demon-the-decent-moments","id":605017,"title":"What are you best Demon the Decent Moments ?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-27T14:52:02-07:00","id":605017,"title":"What are you best Demon the Decent Moments ?","content":"Hello everyone I wanted to create a threat were people could post there best demon the decent game moments. <br /> <br /> It might give others ideas and just show how awesome the game is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T17:23:09-07:00","id":605139,"title":"","content":"Haven't run an excess of Demon, but certainly the most memorable use of Demonic powers was when my player went Loud, the used echoing death...on himself. Creating a Paradox where he killed himself, but erased the act of going loud and killed himself.<br /> <br /> I ended up ruling that he survived, with his cover at 1 and a permanent Catastrophic Glitch, but free of all God-Machine surveillance (because he profoundly screwed up the system). A reward for out of the box thinking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 07-27-2015, 08:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T17:52:03-07:00","id":605150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/605017-what-are-you-best-demon-the-decent-moments?p=605139#post605139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Haven't run an excess of Demon, but certainly the most memorable use of Demonic powers was when my player went Loud, the used echoing death...on himself. Creating a Paradox where he killed himself, but erased the act of going loud and killed himself.<br /> <br /> I ended up ruling that he survived, with his cover at 1 and a permanent Catastrophic Glitch, but free of all God-Machine surveillance (because he profoundly screwed up the system). A reward for out of the box thinking.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There's a similar moment in Interface (which provides rules for self-destructing), where a demon explodes and uses Four Minutes Ago to walk away, IIRC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T18:04:33-07:00","id":605157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/605017-what-are-you-best-demon-the-decent-moments?p=605150#post605150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> There's a similar moment in Interface (which provides rules for self-destructing), where a demon explodes and uses Four Minutes Ago to walk away, IIRC.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're mixing up stories; Ashes doesn't have <i>any</i> Exploits and being able to walk away is just a regular function of performing a self-destruct, but there's two different gadgets in the Interface with Four Minutes Ago Installed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T03:31:47-07:00","id":605436,"title":"","content":"My favorite moments? Well, I have a perverse enjoyment out of using Play on Words. Once, challenged someone to a game of Rock, Paper, Scissors. Got them to say that they were Rock. Ended up pausing the game, and had a fun OOC discussion over if I should turn my poor victim into stone temporarily, a rock musician, or something else. <br /> <br /> Perhaps, my favorite parts of the game, though, was whenever we found a new Infrastructure, sitting down with our group's Inquisitor and arguing about the best way to subvert it, and maybe if there was some way to bleed off the energy output into a completely different area through piping it out into a nearby hookah shop. We wanted to convert the aether into something demons could smoke for a boost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T06:19:05-07:00","id":605533,"title":"","content":"A player having to deal with 3 types of angels because he couldn't leave well enough alone. He had a qashmallim warning him off his course of actions, angels hunting him from the aether backlash of his experiments and accidently ended up on the borders of Aether. He was trying to make souls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4090-mental-state","name":"Mental-State","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T15:24:32-07:00","id":606009,"title":"","content":"A player of mine used Four Minutes Ago to blackmail a candidate for Vice President of the United States.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T17:10:29-07:00","id":606088,"title":"","content":"One of the best moments I had was when 2 of the players got captured by a lot of cultists and two demons. They were being held in a church and could not use any of their abilities to escape from where they were being held. The demons were trying to call an angel to their location.<br /> <br /> The player who was leaving the game was the only would go could respond. He was playing a guardian who gave up on being a guardian who spent his days just trying to find happiness but these demons were his friends the only ones he truly trusted so he would once again go to defend someone. After them getting captured he did not know who else to trust so he went in himself. In the rain he walked to the church as the sky opened up and began to pour. He did not sneak in he ripped open the doors to the front of the church and walked in. Inside the church cultists sat in row after row of the pews listening to these demons wax on about how it was time for them to become one with god again.<br /> <br /> He walked down the aisle they all were too busy listening to these demons talk when he got close enough he interrupted there speech by saying &quot;False gods and broken toys childish and its time to put away childish things.&quot;<br /> Using &quot;merciless gunmen&quot; The player rolled and I felt like I was going to die laughing after we saw he rolled a critical success. The player always used twin Glock 18s each one held 20 rounds +1 in the chamber. He leveled all the cultists in a bloody symphony of death. Soon a long battle with two demons happened. It ended with him steal enough anther from one to use hellfire and he dispatched both.<br /> <br /> He saved his cohorts from the basement brining them up to the church just as all the windows broke. The Stain Glass imagine of Jesus shattered a powerful angel descended it was white hot beautiful fury. He told the other two the run as he ripped away his cover going loud to show his true self and fought this thing.<br /> <br /> The game ended with them leaving as the church blew up and they never heard from their friend again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T07:53:27-07:00","id":606573,"title":"","content":"One of my players bought the cultist merit at level 5 and had fame and charisma. The character was a youtube cosplay girl. He had all of his cultist be female and be maids and he used his money to build maid cafes he had all of them train to be soilders so that he could try to cause the cosplay apocalypse.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T08:49:51-07:00","id":606650,"title":"","content":"We've had some fantastic sessions in our game. My character, Mr Armitage, runs a nightclub called Heresies. So far we've had a bail-fleeing bassist called Butterball be decapitated by a flying hubcap, had my associate- who's a psychiatrist- wrangle a grieving man's dead girlfriend off of him as an extra layer of cover, had a frantic gunfight where a bookie ended up shot in the foot and had Armitage and friends take part in a game of Poker (with another Demon, to boot) which resulted in a set of very angry very fleeced players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The phrase 'flies on the heads of pins' appeared 43 times in that journal, sometimes in the middle of sentences or written in the margins.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4871-malkydel","name":"Malkydel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4871_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T22:59:50-07:00","id":641161,"title":"","content":"One of the characters in our group is married to a VASCU agent. Last session, a slasher based on Kevin Spacy's &quot;John Doe&quot; from Se7en decides to do the classic &quot;I have your wife and child&quot; trope. The Serial Killer arrives at the apartment... and immediately takes eight bullets to the face. All well and dandy, except that there is no way the character's Cover (an Air Force desk officer) can explain how she deftly put down a serial killer who had eluded the FBI dragnet.<br /> <br /> Her solution? Fake her own kidnapping, drag John Doe's headless corpse around the city using embeds to create the illusion that JD is still alive, and leaving clues for the FBI task force to follow. She then arranges a showdown where the VASCU pumps John Doe corpse full of lead in abandoned warehouse, then allows her self to be &quot;rescued&quot; shortly thereafter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","user":"Agentwestmer","date":". 08-27-2015, 01:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T18:51:08-07:00","id":644820,"title":"","content":"At the end of our first story. The ring split up. Two demons hunted down a cryptid rat king/ queen that had Been reproducing a swarm unchecked and was now a threat since they were running out of an easy source of aether so were now targeting demons. <br /> Anyways the demons. Mr. Blaze and mr. Price tracked the rat king/queen into a heavily secured and occupied nest. With some clever use of play on words and cause and effect mr. Price manages to get through the defenses and towards the horde. Mr. Blaze steps in and acts upon his name sake. You can imagine the fire related form abilities, embeds, and exploits he brings to the fray. Mr. Price can fight. But he does not. That's all well in good. After the burning battle with mr. Blaze taking a few nasty hits he uses four minutes ago. Sending everything back to the point where mr. Price used cause and effect to break into the deepest part of the layer. This time the effect sent off a chain with faulty wiring and a gas main dealing with the cryptid threat in another bout of hellish flame. <br /> Mr blaze returns returns to the scene with a very smug mr. Price playing up the fact he dealt with the major threat without getting his hands dirty. Mr blaze being a great sport because it's in his nature. To get to burn anything related to the god machine that doesn't fit his needs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}